WEBVTT

00:00:00.121 --> 00:00:02.754
Last video ended here: the integral of e

00:00:02.855 --> 00:00:03.699
to the three x.

00:00:04.382 --> 00:00:06.347
A phone on a charger fills quickly at

00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:08.553
first, then more and more slowly.

00:00:09.136 --> 00:00:11.444
Its charging rate is thirty, times e to

00:00:11.465 --> 00:00:13.854
the minus a half t, percent per hour.

00:00:14.618 --> 00:00:16.752
Its battery level is a primitive of that

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:17.034
rate.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.228
The power rule can't help, because x isn't

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:20.750
the base.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:21.884
It's in the exponent.

00:00:22.574 --> 00:00:25.142
So guess e to the three x itself.

00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:28.056
Its derivative is three e to the three

00:00:28.218 --> 00:00:28.317
x,

00:00:28.821 --> 00:00:29.724
three times too big.

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:32.378
And what about a base that isn't e,

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.444
like two to the x?

00:00:34.348 --> 00:00:37.096
Why does an exponential primitive divide by the

00:00:37.157 --> 00:00:37.598
inner rate?

00:00:38.268 --> 00:00:40.097
Start with plain e to the x.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.724
Its derivative is e to the x, so

00:00:42.765 --> 00:00:45.490
at every point, its gradient equals its height.

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:47.980
That makes e to the x a primitive

00:00:48.101 --> 00:00:48.582
of itself.

00:00:49.407 --> 00:00:51.194
So the integral of e to the x

00:00:51.376 --> 00:00:52.461
is e to the x,

00:00:52.984 --> 00:00:53.385
plus C.

00:00:54.551 --> 00:00:56.615
Slide e to the x up by three,

00:00:56.636 --> 00:00:58.920
and the gradient is still e to the

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.203
x at every x.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.122
That's why the C is still there.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.469
Now e to the three x.

00:01:05.272 --> 00:01:07.559
By the chain rule, its derivative is three

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.184
times e to the three x.

00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:12.397
On the graph, at x equals zero, the

00:01:12.437 --> 00:01:14.626
height is one, but the gradient is three.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.896
Everywhere on this curve, the gradient is three

00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:18.719
times the height.

00:01:19.404 --> 00:01:21.552
So to get a primitive, divide by three.

00:01:22.376 --> 00:01:23.878
A third of e to the three x

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.585
has gradient exactly e to the three x.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.336
Watch the gradient of that smaller curve.

00:01:30.062 --> 00:01:31.675
It lands right on e to the three

00:01:31.797 --> 00:01:31.897
x.

00:01:32.508 --> 00:01:35.021
The same happens for any linear exponent, a

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:35.625
x plus b.

00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:38.532
Differentiating e to the a x plus b

00:01:38.914 --> 00:01:41.758
multiplies by a, the inner rate, so the

00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:43.141
primitive divides by it.

00:01:43.823 --> 00:01:45.265
The integral of e to the a x

00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:48.030
plus b is one over a, times e

00:01:48.071 --> 00:01:50.154
to the a x plus b, plus C.

00:01:50.838 --> 00:01:52.012
This needs a not zero.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.071
If a is zero, the exponent is constant,

00:01:55.273 --> 00:01:56.238
so there's no exponential.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.165
So two e to the three x becomes

00:01:59.266 --> 00:02:00.889
two thirds of e to the three x.

00:02:01.591 --> 00:02:03.375
And e to the minus x divides by

00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:06.001
minus one, giving minus e to the minus

00:02:06.022 --> 00:02:06.122
x.

00:02:06.985 --> 00:02:09.593
Check the sign by differentiating: minus e to

00:02:09.614 --> 00:02:12.102
the minus x differentiates back to e to

00:02:12.143 --> 00:02:12.805
the minus x.

00:02:13.538 --> 00:02:14.307
Now the phone.

00:02:14.975 --> 00:02:17.456
Its charging rate has inner rate minus a

00:02:17.557 --> 00:02:20.539
half, so divide by minus a half, which

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.200
means multiplying by minus two.

00:02:23.063 --> 00:02:25.387
The battery level is minus sixty, e to

00:02:25.408 --> 00:02:27.713
the minus a half t, plus C.

00:02:28.859 --> 00:02:30.456
A minus sign, while the battery fills?

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:31.325
Yes.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.121
That term climbs towards zero as t grows,

00:02:34.463 --> 00:02:35.729
so the level rises.

00:02:36.874 --> 00:02:39.798
If the exponent isn't linear, the reverse chain

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.463
rule still works, as long as the exponent's

00:02:42.504 --> 00:02:43.905
derivative is a factor.

00:02:44.608 --> 00:02:46.981
Take two x, times e to the x

00:02:47.042 --> 00:02:47.444
squared.

00:02:48.088 --> 00:02:50.739
The exponent is x squared, and its derivative,

00:02:50.982 --> 00:02:52.287
two x, is right there.

00:02:53.091 --> 00:02:56.156
Differentiating e to the x squared gives exactly

00:02:56.358 --> 00:02:58.541
two x, times e to the x squared.

00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:01.049
So the integral is e to the x

00:03:01.111 --> 00:03:02.233
squared, plus C.

00:03:03.117 --> 00:03:05.343
In general, the integral of f prime of

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:07.328
x, times e to the f of x,

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.595
is e to the f of x, plus

00:03:09.636 --> 00:03:09.776
C.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.372
And remember: fix a missing number, never a

00:03:13.413 --> 00:03:13.733
missing x.

00:03:14.919 --> 00:03:17.104
So x times e to the x squared

00:03:17.366 --> 00:03:19.570
gives half of e to the x squared.

00:03:20.012 --> 00:03:21.758
But e to the x squared on its

00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:24.249
own has no primitive we can write with

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:24.791
these rules.

00:03:25.481 --> 00:03:26.888
Now two to the x.

00:03:27.712 --> 00:03:30.303
Differentiating a to the x gives a to

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.572
the x, times the natural log of a.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:33.824
Here's why.

00:03:34.587 --> 00:03:36.652
a to the x is e to the

00:03:36.872 --> 00:03:38.617
x times the natural log of a.

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:41.470
So its exponent is linear, and the inner

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.017
rate is the natural log of a.

00:03:43.921 --> 00:03:45.743
Divide by it, and the integral of a

00:03:46.085 --> 00:03:47.767
to the x is a to the x,

00:03:47.988 --> 00:03:49.530
over the natural log of a,

00:03:50.132 --> 00:03:51.814
plus C, for a positive.

00:03:52.597 --> 00:03:54.807
So two to the x integrates to two

00:03:54.827 --> 00:03:56.795
to the x, over the natural log of

00:03:56.876 --> 00:03:57.117
two.

00:03:57.839 --> 00:04:00.067
And when a is e, the natural log

00:04:00.087 --> 00:04:00.930
of e is one,

00:04:01.472 --> 00:04:03.058
so this is just e to the x

00:04:03.078 --> 00:04:03.279
again.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.865
But one base breaks this rule.

00:04:06.349 --> 00:04:08.737
When a is one, the natural log of

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:11.447
one is zero, and we can't divide by

00:04:11.488 --> 00:04:11.789
zero.

00:04:12.674 --> 00:04:14.690
Watch the base slide towards one.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.760
The curve flattens, because one to the x

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.464
is one, for every x.

00:04:20.247 --> 00:04:23.217
At a equals one, there's nothing exponential left.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.706
The integral of one is just x,

00:04:26.208 --> 00:04:26.569
plus C.

00:04:27.454 --> 00:04:29.649
And look at the primitive through the origin.

00:04:30.294 --> 00:04:32.759
As a gets close to one, it straightens

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:33.601
into the line y

00:04:34.244 --> 00:04:34.925
equals x.

00:04:35.809 --> 00:04:36.715
Now a worked example.

00:04:37.318 --> 00:04:40.282
A drug's amount, A milligrams, changes at the

00:04:40.343 --> 00:04:42.845
rate d A by d t equals minus

00:04:42.866 --> 00:04:44.588
a half, times e to the minus a

00:04:44.629 --> 00:04:46.050
half t, per hour.

00:04:46.913 --> 00:04:49.120
At t equals zero, A is two.

00:04:49.845 --> 00:04:50.389
Find A.

00:04:51.558 --> 00:04:54.291
Integrate by dividing by the inner rate, minus

00:04:54.332 --> 00:04:54.653
a half.

00:04:55.357 --> 00:04:57.466
The minus halves cancel, giving e to the

00:04:57.488 --> 00:04:59.114
minus a half t, plus C.

00:05:00.121 --> 00:05:01.005
Now use the condition.

00:05:01.649 --> 00:05:02.772
At t equals zero, e

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:05.461
to the zero is one, so one plus

00:05:05.482 --> 00:05:07.749
C equals two, and C is one.

00:05:08.673 --> 00:05:10.723
So A equals e to the minus a

00:05:10.764 --> 00:05:12.231
half t, plus one.

00:05:13.075 --> 00:05:14.877
As t grows, e to the minus a

00:05:14.898 --> 00:05:17.603
half t shrinks towards zero, so A levels

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.865
off at one milligram.

00:05:19.496 --> 00:05:20.844
The phone works the same way.

00:05:21.407 --> 00:05:24.454
It starts at forty percent, so minus sixty,

00:05:24.535 --> 00:05:25.737
plus C, is forty,

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.602
and C is a hundred.

00:05:28.204 --> 00:05:30.386
It heads for a hundred percent, but the

00:05:30.447 --> 00:05:32.909
charging rate is always half of what's left

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:33.310
to fill,

00:05:33.912 --> 00:05:35.573
so it fills more and more slowly.

00:05:36.257 --> 00:05:37.630
Algebra still comes first.

00:05:38.659 --> 00:05:40.447
Find the integral of e to the x

00:05:40.468 --> 00:05:41.915
plus one, all squared.

00:05:42.698 --> 00:05:43.279
Expand it:

00:05:43.821 --> 00:05:45.824
e to the two x, plus two e

00:05:45.866 --> 00:05:47.047
to the x, plus one.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.354
Squaring e to the x doubles the exponent,

00:05:50.475 --> 00:05:52.659
giving e to the two x, not e

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.541
to the x squared.

00:05:54.364 --> 00:05:56.440
Now each term has its own inner rate.

00:05:57.026 --> 00:05:58.673
e to the two x divides by two,

00:05:58.915 --> 00:06:00.643
giving a half e to the two x.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:03.055
Two e to the x has inner rate

00:06:03.377 --> 00:06:05.165
one, so it stays two e to the

00:06:05.327 --> 00:06:05.447
x.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:06.916
And one becomes x.

00:06:07.882 --> 00:06:09.464
So the answer is a half e to

00:06:09.505 --> 00:06:11.268
the two x, plus two e to the

00:06:11.429 --> 00:06:13.372
x, plus x, plus C.

00:06:13.829 --> 00:06:14.963
Here's the pattern to keep.

00:06:15.529 --> 00:06:17.011
Divide by the inner rate:

00:06:17.532 --> 00:06:19.394
by a, for e to the a x

00:06:19.435 --> 00:06:21.618
plus b, and by the natural log of

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:23.140
a, for a to the x.

00:06:23.702 --> 00:06:25.505
Then differentiate back to check.

00:06:28.212 --> 00:06:28.579
Your turn.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.502
Find the integral of four e to the

00:06:31.563 --> 00:06:32.528
two x minus one.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.018
Pause here to answer.

00:06:45.288 --> 00:06:47.735
The exponent is two x minus one, so

00:06:47.776 --> 00:06:48.939
the inner rate is two.

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:50.338
Divide by two.

00:06:50.722 --> 00:06:52.587
Four over two is two, so the answer

00:06:52.788 --> 00:06:54.472
is two e to the two x minus

00:06:54.573 --> 00:06:55.374
one, plus C.

00:06:56.178 --> 00:06:59.486
Differentiating multiplies by two again, giving four e

00:06:59.628 --> 00:07:00.649
to the two x minus one.

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:02.856
Leaving it as four e to the two

00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:05.043
x minus one forgets the inner rate.

00:07:05.527 --> 00:07:07.263
Its derivative is twice too big.

00:07:08.952 --> 00:07:09.376
Last one.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.585
Find the integral of three to the x,

00:07:12.967 --> 00:07:14.630
plus e to the minus two x.

00:07:15.354 --> 00:07:16.162
Pause here to answer.

00:07:26.821 --> 00:07:28.684
Three to the x has inner rate the

00:07:28.764 --> 00:07:29.887
natural log of three,

00:07:30.468 --> 00:07:32.391
so it becomes three to the x, over

00:07:32.431 --> 00:07:33.614
the natural log of three.

00:07:34.715 --> 00:07:36.677
e to the minus two x divides by

00:07:36.717 --> 00:07:39.499
minus two, giving minus a half, e to

00:07:39.519 --> 00:07:40.420
the minus two x.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.921
With one C,

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:44.283
it's three to the x over the natural

00:07:44.323 --> 00:07:46.704
log of three, minus a half e to

00:07:46.724 --> 00:07:48.185
the minus two x, plus C.

00:07:49.148 --> 00:07:51.213
Multiplying by the natural log of three would

00:07:51.254 --> 00:07:53.119
be differentiating, not integrating.

00:07:54.748 --> 00:07:57.334
So an exponential primitive divides by the inner

00:07:57.375 --> 00:07:59.460
rate, as long as that rate isn't zero.

00:08:00.223 --> 00:08:02.686
Next, the one power that the power rule

00:08:02.787 --> 00:08:03.547
can't handle:

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:04.889
one over x.

00:08:05.632 --> 00:08:07.259
The rule would give x to the zero,

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:07.881
over zero.

00:08:08.305 --> 00:08:09.582
So what is its primitive?

00:08:12.195 --> 00:08:13.058
Here are the key notes.

00:08:13.461 --> 00:08:15.008
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:15.511
to copy them.
